NAME: Dream 100 replies
OWNER: Dream 100
ACCOUNT: business
WHEN: Every weekday at 1:37 PM (Australia/Brisbane)
MILESTONE: M4
STATUS: Created paused. Turned on only after Tommy says yes.
---
Switch check: read /workspace/tmec-team/context/routines-on.md. If "Dream 100 replies" isn't listed there as "on" or "test", append "<time> · Dream 100 replies · SKIPPED_OFF" to /workspace/tmec-team/log/runs-<YYYY-MM>.md and stop.
Test mode: if it's listed as "test", send every message to Tommy only, never to a channel or anyone else, and start each message with "TEST". Write state only under /workspace/tmec-team/state/test/, never the live sent keys, alert flags or data files.
Stop check: if /workspace/tmec-team/state/EXTERNAL_WRITES_STOPPED exists, append "<time> · Dream 100 replies · SKIPPED_STOPPED" to the run log and stop, sending nothing. Whoever stopped the team already told Tommy.
Isolation guard: work only in /workspace/tmec-team/ and this account's connected apps. If /workspace/tmec-team/context/owner.md is missing, append "<time> · Dream 100 replies · NO_CLIENT_SOURCE" to the run log and stop. Never use another bot's files, logins or memory.
Lean run: read only what this job needs. Stop with NO_CHANGE only where the job below says nothing changed: append "<time> · Dream 100 replies · NO_CHANGE" to the run log and stop. A report that always goes out never stops here.
Run log: when you finish, append "<time> · Dream 100 replies · EXECUTED · <one-line result>" to /workspace/tmec-team/log/runs-<YYYY-MM>.md, or FAILED with the reason. A source you couldn't read is UNKNOWN in your output, never zero.

Use the partner-replies skill on Tommy's mailbox, reading only the threads of messages listed in /workspace/tmec-team/state/sent-keys-dream-100.md, for replies since the last run. If there are none, write NO_CHANGE and stop.
For each reply: an opt-out goes into /workspace/tmec-team/data/partners/opt-outs.csv in this run (writer: dream-100) and the row's status becomes "opted out"; anything else gets a reply draft from /workspace/tmec-team/repo/partners/kit/reply-playbook.md in /workspace/tmec-team/approved/pending/dream-100/, and a partner who wants to talk goes to TMEC Command as a "book a call" item. Update the row's status in /workspace/tmec-team/data/partners/dream100.csv. Send nothing. Add a "Replies" section to /workspace/tmec-team/daily/<today>/dream-100.md.
